<https://github.com/corrado877/CognitiveBiasOntologies/blob/main/Masked_man_fallacy/Masked_Man_Fallacy.owl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Masked Man fallacy, also known as the Illicit Substitution of Identicals, is a cognitive bias where people mistakenly reject two names as referring to the same person or thing if one of the names involves a description or characteristic. This occurs because people tend to treat names as rigid designators and fail to recognize that a masked or described name can refer to the same entity."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
