<https://dbpedia.org/resource/Knowledge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Knowledge can be defined as awareness of facts or as practical skills, and may also refer to familiarity with objects or situations. Knowledge of facts, also called propositional knowledge, is often defined as true belief that is distinct from opinion or guesswork by virtue of justification."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
_:Nf17be02dd6aa443d9ba1acdba372ceda <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://github.com/corrado877/CognitiveBiasOntologies/blob/main/CognitiveBiasOntologies#rejects> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The act of denying a particular intention in favour of one or more others."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
