<https://dbpedia.org/resource/Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An entity is something that exists as itself, as a subject or as an object, actually or potentially, concretely or abstractly, physically or not. It need not be of material existence. In particular, abstractions and legal fictions are usually regarded as entities. In general, there is also no presumption that an entity is animate, or present. The adjectival form is entitative."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
